{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And this for Judah.</b> So too he said concerning Judah that he shall live and not die, and he further added: Hear, O HaShem, the voice of Judah when he comes to battle, for he goes up first." "<b>And to his people You shall bring him.</b> To the camp that was at Gilgal. Or it is a prayer for those who go out to fight against the land of the enemy." "<b>Rav lo.</b> His hands suffice him, and he has no need for someone to help him, but only the help of HaShem alone. Others say it is from the root of ריבה, and the meaning is: his hands shall contend for him. And others said, like וברקים רב, from the root רבו."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {2 "The verse cited fragment 'וברקים רב' appears to be from Psalms; Ibn Ezra's manuscripts vary on the exact citation; rendered as found."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:23.668718509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}